  CardStory: "Twain takes his tea with a nice dollop of honey. It calms hims, he
    says.\r\n\r\nHe hasn\u2019t taken his earliest weeks in the Order well. Secunda
    sits next to him in the mess hall every day at the exact same time, early evening.
    She is surprisingly punctual, for someone who is always being chewed out for
    lack of discipline. She\u2019s a Club, and the research division officers rarely
    have patience for slackers.\r\n\r\nSecunda always seems to get away with it\r\n\r\nThey
    drink tea together, but no sugar for her. Secunda hates sugar.\r\n\r\nThis, he
    knows full well. She mentioned it when they were in basic, and it stuck in Twain\u2019s
    brain. Like many other things about Secunda. It is easy to think about her. Comfortable. "
